{"items":[{"owner":{"reputation":717,"user_id":7887334,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":62,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/fb530ca79afcb037bb895f2a56c9b8c0?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Clay","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/7887334/clay"},"is_accepted":false,"score":0,"last_activity_date":1505531365,"last_edit_date":1505531365,"creation_date":1505529876,"answer_id":46249567,"question_id":31943174,"body_markdown":"I used cx_freeze for a project at work.  I&#39;m not sure if this is your problem... but I was using the Anaconda distribution, and cx_freeze was not properly gathering the .dll&#39;s that I needed for my project.\r\n\r\nThe solution was to:\r\n\r\n1. Install a plane version of Python\r\n2. make an environment with the packages that I needed for that project\r\n3. Run cx_freeze.\r\n\r\nMagically, all of the problems went away and everything compiled like it was supposed too."},{"owner":{"reputation":1,"user_id":9004067,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/573ee968096520cb87cc29bd6a05105e?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Namah Jain","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/9004067/namah-jain"},"is_accepted":false,"score":0,"last_activity_date":1511535341,"creation_date":1511535341,"answer_id":47475733,"question_id":31943174,"body_markdown":"Well the problem you are facing may be due to the lack of dependencies.\r\ncx_Freeze have some dependencies.\r\nIn order to distribute your work in python many lightweight packages are avalible.\r\nYou can use:-\r\n\r\n 1. Pyinstaller: it can be installed by\r\n\r\n   pip install pyinstaller\r\n   pyinstaller is really good for making  executables with less size\r\n\r\n 2. Py2exe\r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\n\r\n  "},{"owner":{"reputation":173722,"user_id":99834,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":46,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/0kMIVmSC.png?s=256","display_name":"sorin","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/99834/sorin"},"is_accepted":false,"score":-1,"last_activity_date":1464538918,"creation_date":1464538918,"answer_id":37512217,"question_id":31943174,"body_markdown":"I know that probably this is not what you want to hear, but the reality is that you will never be able to succeed with this approach and here is why:\r\n\r\n* Linux does not have portably Python package binaries, meaning that a compiled numpy on one distro will probably not work on another. It can even happen with the same distribution and version, just because one system library received an update.\r\n* [manylinux1](https://github.com/pypa/manylinux) is supposed to solve this but is really hard to build packages for it and only few started using it.\r\n* cx-freeze project had latest release in December 2014, which on Python timescale puts it as an abandoned project."}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":223}
